# Guard for build-tarball's conditional patch application.
# Format: [!]<relpath-in-tarball>:<grep -E regex>   (ALL lines must hold)
# A leading '!' negates (the pattern must NOT be present).
#
# 0012 synthesises BLK_STS_P2PDMA for member completions on kernels whose
# block layer cannot produce it. Both predicates below must hold, because the
# patch needs BOTH shapes present in the tree:
#
#  * raid1_write_error() -- upstream's v6 completion handling, which is what
#    0012's early-return/dispatch hunks are written against. It is absent on
#    the bare upstream `master` baseline TODAY, but v6 p5 introduces it, so
#    once the series merges a plain upstream tree satisfies this line alone.
#
#  * raid1_can_advertise_p2pdma() -- the meshstor member-AND advertise helper.
#    Permanently meshstor-only: upstream has no member-AND policy and no plan
#    for one, so this is the predicate that keeps 0012 off a bare-upstream
#    baseline for good. It is not decoration: hunk #2 of raid1.c anchors its
#    trailing context on raid1_p2pdma_is_advertising(), which only exists
#    alongside that helper, so on an upstream+v6 tree the hunk would hard
#    reject and fail bin/build-tarball. 0008/0009/0010 and the dkms selftests
#    key on the same helper for the same reason.
raid1-10.c:raid1_write_error
raid1-10.c:raid1_can_advertise_p2pdma
